            <ArticleTitle>[Ectopic ossification as a cause of vague abdominal pain following heart surgery: a case report].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>684-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Vague abdominal pain after cardiac surgery was caused by ectopic ossification in the distal part of sternotomy. The rarity of this complication (one case seen in recent years, operation volume: 1200 cases/year) prompted us to review the literature, where only 6 cases are described. Diagnostic problems and therapy are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
